src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@finsweet/attributes@2/attributes.js"
fs-inject
></script><!-- Hero first paint. The hero and composer must be complete in the first frame:
     1. The desktop scroll interaction (i-872ba3c7) makes Webflow hide .p-hero-header_content
        until IX3 boots at the end of the page. It starts at "top top", so its from-state is
        scale 1 and showing the hero early changes nothing.
     2. relume-anim's blur-fade would otherwise hide the hero again at DOMContentLoaded.
     3. Copies of the CSS that ComposerTabsCss, ComposerCaretCss, ComposerAttachCss and
        ComposerHomeCss inject from the end of <body>. Update both when those change.
     4. On tablet/desktop the hero video's poster is the LCP element. It sits in a <video>
        deep in the body, so without this the browser only finds it once the parser gets
        there, at normal priority. On phones the LCP is the H1 instead, so the media query
        keeps this from competing with the CSS there. Keep this URL in step with the poster
        in #publish-hero-video (rules/hero-video.md).
     5. relume-anim's stylesheet. This page used to apply the registered RelumeAnimBoot
        1.2.1 (relume-anim-boot-v2b.js), a render-blocking request whose only jobs were a
        duplicate of the site head's theme boot and injecting this stylesheet. The
        stylesheet is injected inline instead (perf, 2026-10-24) - still script-inserted,
        so still non-blocking, exactly as before. If RelumeAnimBoot moves to a new CSS
        file, change this URL with it. -->
<script>(function(){var l=document.createElement('link');l.rel='stylesheet';l.href='https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6177739448baa66404ce1d9c/6a829c94a7b6a5ef6a03fdce_relume-anim-v22.css';document.head.appendChild(l);})();</script>
