bsite-files.com/6177739448baa66404ce1d9c/6a83bfceb4fddc20e92325ed_cp-publish-main-v2-p-1080.webp 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6177739448baa66404ce1d9c/6a83bfceb4fddc20e92325ed_cp-publish-main-v2.webp 1266w"/><div id="choose-path-publish-shot" class="w-embed w-script"><!-- Publish product shot, cropped to this card — Figma 2605:72523.
     The same asset as the hero: derived from publish-hero-v5.js with its `rph`
     namespace renamed to `cpp` so the two stylesheets cannot collide. The three
     style guides, the guide switching, the lazy photograph hydration, the intro
     rise and dark mode all carry over untouched.

     Three things are its own. The crop: the artboard is 1.42x this slot's width
     and hangs off its left edge, so the card shows through above, below and to
     the right of it. The stacking: the shot carries position relative and
     z-index 1, the same as the `.choose-path_image` it stands in for, so the
     Publish Grid Pattern in `.p-grid-wrapper` stays behind it and keeps
     switching with dark mode. And the shot's one change — the nav's Publish
     button is filled with background/ai-bold #ff00f4 instead of being stroked.

     The image above this is canvas-only, so it is what the Designer shows and
     the shot is what ships. Its margins are transparent so the grid reads
     through it on the canvas too. Delete this element to revert to the image.

     v3 (2026-10-24, perf): builds only the snapshot on show; the other two are
     built when someone reaches for the shot. Loaded after the page (it is below
     the fold) via the site head's __rlAfterLoadScript, falling back to a plain
     load if that helper is ever missing. -->
<div data-relume-choose-path-publish></div>
